1
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:00,479
Yan'er, let me tell you.

2
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:02,880
Not watching the Spring Festival Gala...

3
00:01:03,479 --> 00:01:05,239
is like eating dumplings without vinegar.

4
00:01:05,239 --> 00:01:06,439
What's the difference?

5
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:07,680
Right?

6
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:09,959
It's not like we can't afford it.

7
00:01:10,519 --> 00:01:11,439
Right, Yan'er?

8
00:01:13,159 --> 00:01:14,280
Yan'er?

9
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:17,920
Yan'er?

10
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:26,640
Yan'er?

11
00:01:27,799 --> 00:01:29,400
Don't test me like this.

12
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:31,760
I might not be able to hold back.

13
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:33,599
After all,

14
00:01:34,879 --> 00:01:35,920
I'm only human.

15
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,280
Look what I've done...

16
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:04,599
What a mess.

17
00:02:04,599 --> 00:02:05,760
I'm worse than a beast.

18
00:02:05,799 --> 00:02:07,040
A complete beast, honestly.

19
00:02:07,519 --> 00:02:08,639
What was I thinking?

20
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,680
It's all on me.

21
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:11,879
Last night,

22
00:02:13,159 --> 00:02:14,400
I had a bit too much cheap booze,

23
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:15,879
and blacked out completely.

24
00:02:15,879 --> 00:02:16,599
My brain is just...

25
00:02:16,599 --> 00:02:17,840
All day long, my head is just

26
00:02:18,719 --> 00:02:20,400
like shoddy construction,

27
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,080
like it's made of paper,

28
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:21,960
shattering at the slightest tap.

29
00:02:22,599 --> 00:02:23,719
Total piece of junk.

30
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,719
Please don't be mad.

31
00:02:30,719 --> 00:02:31,879
If you still feel like

32
00:02:32,599 --> 00:02:33,400
you can't let it go,

33
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,599
go ahead and curse me out,

34
00:02:34,599 --> 00:02:35,439
hit me a few times,

35
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:36,639
I'll even get down on my knees.

36
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:38,400
I swear I will.

37
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:41,479
No, really...

38
00:02:42,759 --> 00:02:43,319
Look at me,

39
00:02:45,159 --> 00:02:46,400
my voice when I talk to you,

40
00:02:46,599 --> 00:02:47,560
it's literally shaking.

41
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:48,240
My voice is even...

42
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:50,080
Not that I'm scared of you,

43
00:02:50,159 --> 00:02:51,120
or scared you'll report me.

44
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:51,919
It's mainly that

45
00:02:53,159 --> 00:02:54,520
I hate to see you hurt.

46
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:58,479
Things between a man and a woman,

47
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,599
there's really no explaining it.

48
00:03:02,159 --> 00:03:03,120
What can you do?

49
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:03,759
When two people

50
00:03:04,439 --> 00:03:05,120
are together for so long,

51
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:06,120
feelings just grow.

52
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,719
Besides, you're just so...

53
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:11,000
so good-looking.

54
00:03:11,439 --> 00:03:12,520
You're more irresistible the more I look.

55
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:15,879
No man could hold back.

56
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:17,759
Who could resist that?

57
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,120
Why are you leaving already?

58
00:03:21,479 --> 00:03:21,800
Yan'er!

59
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:22,680
Wait,

60
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:24,479
I already know what to buy for breakfast.

61
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:25,719
How about soy milk and fried dough?

62
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,599
What kind of acting is this?

63
00:03:32,639 --> 00:03:34,080
The acting is so fake.

64
00:03:35,159 --> 00:03:36,159
Look at how that woman cries,

65
00:03:36,159 --> 00:03:37,680
like squeezing out toothpaste.

66
00:03:37,919 --> 00:03:38,919
Actors have to make it real.

67
00:03:38,919 --> 00:03:39,680
Even you'd do better.

68
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:40,520
With your pretty face,

69
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:41,960
just standing there you'd beat her.

70
00:03:42,439 --> 00:03:43,479
If only I had the cash.

71
00:03:43,479 --> 00:03:44,800
I'd send you to Shudian,

72
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:45,599
and you'd be a star for sure.

73
00:03:45,759 --> 00:03:46,479
"Shudian"?

74
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:47,919
It's called Hengdian.

75
00:03:48,439 --> 00:03:49,120
Hengdian, right.

76
00:03:51,199 --> 00:03:51,879
I'm not acting.

77
00:03:51,879 --> 00:03:52,800
I'm no actress.

78
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,680
You just lack a talent scout, really.

79
00:03:55,759 --> 00:03:57,400
If one found you, you'd be famous by now.

80
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:00,240
Let's act together.

81
00:04:01,039 --> 00:04:01,919
Tell you what,

82
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:03,719
let's act out

83
00:04:05,439 --> 00:04:07,800
Romeo and Juliet in the slums.

84
00:04:08,599 --> 00:04:10,280
We might not have a candlelit dinner,

85
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,319
but we've got a light bulb.

86
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,400
We might not have wine glasses,

87
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,919
but we've got true love.

88
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:17,680
Come on, my leading lady.

89
00:04:18,759 --> 00:04:19,120
Have a sip.

90
00:04:19,279 --> 00:04:19,800
I don't want to drink.

91
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:21,160
Be good.

92
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,040
I'm not drinking.

93
00:04:22,279 --> 00:04:22,759
Just one sip.

94
00:04:22,759 --> 00:04:23,839
Just one sip, come on.

95
00:04:24,279 --> 00:04:25,040
Fine, I'll take a sip.

96
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:31,600
It tastes awful.

97
00:04:44,959 --> 00:04:46,120
I'm watching TV.

98
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:48,360
Stop it.

99
00:04:48,839 --> 00:04:49,399
Watching TV?

100
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:54,759
I can't wait anymore.

101
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:57,920
The male lead is way too into character.

102
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:00,360
I've got inspiration right now.

103
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:01,920
It'll be gone in a second.

104
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:03,319
Come over here, my Yan'er.

105
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,279
Stop it.

106
00:05:09,319 --> 00:05:11,199
I just had some cheap booze last night.

107
00:05:11,199 --> 00:05:12,920
How could I be...

108
00:05:12,959 --> 00:05:13,759
how could I just be...

109
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:15,319
such a bastard?

110
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:17,959
Stop packing.

111
00:05:18,079 --> 00:05:19,199
I just had a few drinks.

112
00:05:19,839 --> 00:05:21,120
Every blow that landed on you...

113
00:05:21,319 --> 00:05:22,600
it broke my own heart.

114
00:05:22,879 --> 00:05:24,720
My heart feels pricked with needles,

115
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:26,000
aching so deeply.

116
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,240
Look at you, staying silent again.

117
00:05:27,639 --> 00:05:28,199
When you don't speak,

118
00:05:28,199 --> 00:05:29,680
the whole mood in this room feels off.

119
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,120
It wasn't easy for us

120
00:05:31,519 --> 00:05:32,839
to build this cozy little home.

121
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:35,199
Don't leave.

122
00:05:35,199 --> 00:05:36,240
Stop packing your things, Yan'er.

123
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:36,959
Listen to me.

124
00:05:36,959 --> 00:05:37,720
Our destiny...

125
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:38,800
it's not like other people's.

126
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:39,720
The God of Marriage

127
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:41,319
welded us together with steel rebar.

128
00:05:41,759 --> 00:05:42,879
We can't just throw it away.

129
00:05:42,879 --> 00:05:44,240
Give me one more chance.

130
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:45,079
Can you?

131
00:05:45,079 --> 00:05:45,680
If I don't change this time,

132
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,519
I'm the biggest bastard alive.

133
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,959
How many chances have I given you, Qiangzi?

134
00:05:52,079 --> 00:05:52,959
We're through.

135
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:54,600
Let's part on good terms.

136
00:05:55,319 --> 00:05:56,120
What?

137
00:05:57,319 --> 00:05:58,519
What do you mean, "part on good terms"?

138
00:05:59,399 --> 00:06:00,639
All these months,

139
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,399
working like a dog for you!

140
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:03,360
You say part on good terms,

141
00:06:03,439 --> 00:06:04,360
and we just part on good terms?

142
00:06:06,319 --> 00:06:07,560
I poured my warm heart into you,

143
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:08,839
and you're still cold as ice?

144
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:11,480
Let me tell you, Han Yan.

145
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:14,399
With me, there is no breaking up.

146
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:15,439
Only widowhood!

147
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:16,079
Come on.

148
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,160
Aren't you leaving?

149
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:19,120
Walk right over my dead body!

150
00:06:57,879 --> 00:06:59,040
Zhang Baokui.

151
00:06:59,959 --> 00:07:01,160
Zhang Baokui.

152
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,759
Come to the village office immediately.

153
00:07:04,759 --> 00:07:07,079
A guy named He Yiqiang is calling you.

154
00:07:38,639 --> 00:07:39,439
You're back.

155
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,199
Are you keeping something from me?

156
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:46,639
Like what?

157
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:50,480
There's a guy.

158
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:52,560
He keeps calling me.

159
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:54,879
Name's He Yiqiang.

160
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:58,439
He says you took something of his.

161
00:07:59,759 --> 00:08:01,279
If you took something from him,

162
00:08:01,279 --> 00:08:02,680
can't we just give it back?

163
00:08:02,959 --> 00:08:05,079
I met him at my last job.

164
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:07,600
He had a thing for me.

165
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:08,639
I ignored him.

166
00:08:11,319 --> 00:08:12,519
And then?

167
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,519
Nothing happened.

168
00:08:15,639 --> 00:08:17,040
He just kept calling,

169
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,120
and I never picked up.

170
00:08:23,079 --> 00:08:24,680
So that was that, right?

171
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:32,200
Where are you going?

172
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,679
Out to work.

173
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,720
Relying on you, I'd starve to death.

174
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:39,600
Don't worry.

175
00:08:39,799 --> 00:08:41,480
I'm going with Sister Zhang this time.

176
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:42,480
She found the job.

177
00:08:43,519 --> 00:08:44,159
Don't worry.

178
00:08:44,879 --> 00:08:45,759
I'm off.

179
00:08:46,759 --> 00:08:47,840
I'll take you there.

180
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,600
No need.

181
00:08:58,799 --> 00:08:59,600
Yanzi!

182
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:04,279
It's not that I don't love you,

183
00:09:04,799 --> 00:09:07,879
it's just that I'm from the countryside.

184
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:10,120
The loose change in my pocket

185
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:12,039
can only buy a pack of cigarettes,

186
00:09:12,039 --> 00:09:15,039
and can't treat you to the good life.

187
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:18,600
I really wanted to work hard,

188
00:09:18,919 --> 00:09:21,919
never backing down no matter how hard.

189
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:25,799
If only you could wait patiently,

190
00:09:25,799 --> 00:09:28,759
I'd marry you once I hit the lottery.

191
00:09:30,519 --> 00:09:32,240
But I can't wait any longer!

192
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,759
I can't live without you, Yanzi!

193
00:09:35,279 --> 00:09:36,000
Yanzi!

194
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,039
I'm scared you'll fly away.

195
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:38,759
If you fly too far, I won't find you!

196
00:09:38,759 --> 00:09:39,519
Look!

197
00:09:39,519 --> 00:09:41,960
I brought everything I own to be with you.

198
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:43,559
I have to be with you!

199
00:09:43,559 --> 00:09:44,639
I love you!

200
00:09:44,799 --> 00:09:45,720
I love you, Yanzi!

201
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:47,000
I love every inch of you!

202
00:09:47,039 --> 00:09:48,080
I love everything about you!

203
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:49,960
Yanzi!

204
00:09:50,559 --> 00:09:51,240
Yanzi!

205
00:09:51,919 --> 00:09:53,200
I knew you'd come downstairs!

206
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,919
You wouldn't ignore me, right?

207
00:09:55,879 --> 00:09:56,559
Come on!

208
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:58,320
Run toward love, Yan'er!

209
00:09:58,759 --> 00:10:00,320
I missed you to death, Yanzi!

210
00:10:03,279 --> 00:10:03,840
Why are you shouting?

211
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:04,639
I'm coming!

212
00:10:04,639 --> 00:10:05,480
Why are you yelling?

213
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:06,559
It's late, everyone's watching!

214
00:10:06,559 --> 00:10:07,240
Are you crazy?

215
00:10:07,879 --> 00:10:09,120
Yeah, I'm crazy!

216
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,799
Crazy in love!

217
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:13,200
Let me tell you,

218
00:10:13,399 --> 00:10:14,080
no matter where you go,

219
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,480
I can find you, believe it or not!

220
00:10:15,639 --> 00:10:16,360
These eyes of mine

221
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:17,200
aren't just for show!

222
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,399
And my sharp nose

223
00:10:18,559 --> 00:10:19,840
is a walking radar!

224
00:10:20,679 --> 00:10:22,919
Unless you fly out of the solar system,

225
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:24,000
otherwise,

226
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:26,200
you can't escape my love's radar!

227
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:27,159
Stop talking!

228
00:10:27,159 --> 00:10:29,039
Come on, let me adore you!

229
00:10:29,039 --> 00:10:29,919
Put me down!

230
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:31,200
Put me down!

231
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:33,240
Put me down!

232
00:10:33,679 --> 00:10:35,039
Everyone is watching!

233
00:10:36,559 --> 00:10:37,639
Put me down!

234
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:40,360
What do you want from me?

235
00:10:41,279 --> 00:10:42,440
Aren't we even?

236
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:44,159
Even? What do you mean even?

237
00:10:44,399 --> 00:10:45,360
I missed you!

238
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:46,799
Whenever I miss you,

239
00:10:46,799 --> 00:10:48,840
all my organs feel twisted up!

240
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,159
You know what I'm like!

241
00:10:50,399 --> 00:10:51,080
Whenever I miss you,

242
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:52,519
these paws of mine

243
00:10:52,519 --> 00:10:53,840
just stop listening to me,

244
00:10:54,039 --> 00:10:55,200
and want to open Taobao

245
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:56,320
to splurge like crazy!

246
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:58,360
Look, I bought all this for you!

247
00:10:58,639 --> 00:10:59,080
This one,

248
00:11:01,279 --> 00:11:02,679
"Soul-Melting Green."

249
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:04,639
You'll look amazing in this!

250
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:05,799
And this one,

251
00:11:05,799 --> 00:11:06,639
doesn't it look pretty?

252
00:11:07,559 --> 00:11:08,879
"Heartbreaking Purple."

253
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:10,120
Super sexy!

254
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:11,080
Once you put it on,

255
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:11,919
They all suit you perfectly!

256
00:11:11,919 --> 00:11:13,159
And this one's the most expensive!

257
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:14,919
This one's truly fierce!

258
00:11:15,399 --> 00:11:15,840
Look,

259
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,120
"Tears of the Fierce Tiger."

260
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:20,759
Won't you look

261
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:21,919
just like a queen in it?

262
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:23,879
Don't be mad anymore.

263
00:11:25,879 --> 00:11:26,519
I swear!

264
00:11:27,519 --> 00:11:29,840
I swear in front of all your coworkers!

265
00:11:30,399 --> 00:11:31,480
I, He Yiqiang,

266
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:32,919
if I ever

267
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:34,480
raise my voice

268
00:11:34,639 --> 00:11:35,960
at Han Yan again,

269
00:11:36,519 --> 00:11:37,399
may I become a mute!

270
00:11:37,919 --> 00:11:39,120
Keep your voice down!

271
00:11:39,639 --> 00:11:40,559
What are you doing?

272
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:42,679
Still mad?

273
00:11:43,519 --> 00:11:44,399
Did you miss me?

274
00:11:45,519 --> 00:11:46,039
Yan'er,

275
00:11:46,759 --> 00:11:48,240
what I did was just

276
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:50,039
an attempted crime at most.

277
00:11:50,679 --> 00:11:52,000
As the honorable judge,

278
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,440
couldn't you give me probation?

279
00:11:53,759 --> 00:11:54,960
Keep observing me,

280
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:55,600
okay?

281
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:57,360
Give me a chance to turn over a new leaf!

282
00:11:59,639 --> 00:12:01,480
Did you gain weight when I picked you up?

283
00:12:02,159 --> 00:12:03,360
Have you been sneaking late-night snacks?

284
00:12:03,879 --> 00:12:04,679
Cut it out!

285
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:07,159
Yan'er!

286
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:11,960
Say, if your husband

287
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:13,519
knew I came here to see you,

288
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:14,600
what could he even do?

289
00:12:15,039 --> 00:12:16,000
Stop talking nonsense.

290
00:12:16,639 --> 00:12:17,279
Don't jinx it.

291
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:20,279
Why get mad the second we're done?

292
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:22,039
Weren't you totally into it just now?

293
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:34,519
Yanzi, open the door. It's me.

294
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:40,840
Coming!

295
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:10,679
He Yiqiang

296
00:13:37,679 --> 00:13:38,360
It's not clean yet.

297
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,320
You're so annoying.

298
00:13:41,639 --> 00:13:42,360
Come in.

299
00:13:46,399 --> 00:13:47,320
What are you doing here?

300
00:13:51,399 --> 00:13:52,440
Who's he?

301
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:53,919
A coworker.

302
00:13:54,759 --> 00:13:55,399
Hurt his leg.

303
00:13:55,639 --> 00:13:57,039
Supervisor told me to look after him.

304
00:13:58,519 --> 00:14:00,159
Why aren't you at work during the day?

305
00:14:00,759 --> 00:14:01,519
I switched shifts.

306
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:02,679
I work tonight.

307
00:14:03,679 --> 00:14:04,480
Who?

308
00:14:04,559 --> 00:14:05,360
My husband.

309
00:14:05,519 --> 00:14:06,320
Your husband?

310
00:14:21,279 --> 00:14:22,200
Give it to me

311
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:40,000
I figure since things have come to this,

312
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,159
let's stop pretending.

313
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:43,320
You know about me and Yan'er, right?

314
00:14:44,759 --> 00:14:45,799
Stop talking nonsense.

315
00:14:46,159 --> 00:14:47,519
It's not your fault,

316
00:14:47,519 --> 00:14:48,120
not Yan'er's either.

317
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,600
None of it is Yan'er's fault.

318
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:51,919
I'm the one who kept pestering her.

319
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,519
She tried to kick me out,

320
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:54,799
she turned me down,

321
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:56,039
but it didn't work.

322
00:14:56,159 --> 00:14:57,799
When I want something,

323
00:14:58,279 --> 00:14:58,879
I don't give up.

324
00:14:58,879 --> 00:14:59,919
So what are you gonna do?

325
00:15:02,279 --> 00:15:03,159
Anyhow,

326
00:15:03,799 --> 00:15:05,320
maybe even God was sick of me.

327
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:09,080
My leg is already like this.

328
00:15:09,679 --> 00:15:11,039
Let's talk about what we do now.

329
00:15:11,879 --> 00:15:12,399
Right?

330
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:14,559
Look ahead.

331
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:16,759
What happens to me?

332
00:15:20,879 --> 00:15:22,039
I did you wrong.

333
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:27,039
So what?

334
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:28,200
No one's gonna look after me?

335
00:15:28,879 --> 00:15:29,480
Am I just...

336
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:30,559
am I supposed to just die here?

337
00:15:30,559 --> 00:15:31,159
Just left on my own?

338
00:15:31,159 --> 00:15:31,960
From now on...

339
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:33,279
Don't talk like that.

340
00:15:33,759 --> 00:15:34,840
Then who's taking care of me?

341
00:15:35,639 --> 00:15:36,480
She can't take care of you.

342
00:15:37,639 --> 00:15:38,240
Can you?

343
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:40,679
You'll do it?

344
00:15:46,759 --> 00:15:47,519
I'll take care of you.

345
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:48,960
What are you talking about?

346
00:15:57,799 --> 00:15:58,799
Quit your job.

347
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:02,159
I'll take him to the fish pond first.

348
00:16:03,039 --> 00:16:04,480
I'll look after him and the fish.

349
00:16:05,879 --> 00:16:07,360
Once his leg heals and he leaves,

350
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:10,200
this will all be behind us.

351
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:11,360
All right?

352
00:16:18,879 --> 00:16:19,679
Brother,

353
00:16:20,919 --> 00:16:23,240
you're a real stand-up guy.

354
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:29,960
What happened next?

355
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:33,039
After that,

356
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:34,879
we kept taking care of him.

357
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:38,360
My husband bought him water,

358
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:40,120
food, cigarettes, and booze.

359
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,080
One day, my husband came home,

360
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:44,360
went straight to sleep without a word.

361
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:47,080
But the next day,

362
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:48,759
my husband told me

363
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,200
it was all over.

364
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:54,799
He said He Yiqiang was gone.

365
00:16:55,759 --> 00:16:56,320
I even asked,

366
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:58,879
"His leg was broken so badly,

367
00:16:58,879 --> 00:16:59,840
how could he leave?"

368
00:17:01,519 --> 00:17:03,919
My husband said he wasn't an orphan,

369
00:17:04,559 --> 00:17:05,559
he had a mother,

370
00:17:06,119 --> 00:17:07,599
and she came and picked him up.

371
00:17:11,319 --> 00:17:12,000
After that,

372
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:14,480
he never reached out to me again,

373
00:17:15,559 --> 00:17:16,799
never called.

374
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:21,680
I really thought it was all behind us.

375
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:33,319
About He Yiqiang's death,

376
00:17:35,359 --> 00:17:36,240
what do you think?

377
00:17:37,599 --> 00:17:38,920
Is he really dead?

378
00:17:40,799 --> 00:17:42,000
He was a bastard.

379
00:17:42,559 --> 00:17:44,519
But when he was with me,

380
00:17:44,799 --> 00:17:46,440
he talked to me more in a single day

381
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,920
than my husband did in a whole year.

382
00:17:49,799 --> 00:17:51,359
What does a woman want anyway?

383
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:54,119
Isn't it just to have someone to talk to?
